{
  "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
  "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Carter G. Phillips (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: There are two issues in this case. One concerns walking time, and the other concerns waiting time. And unless the Court has a different order, I'd propose to start with the walking time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: So, you think Steiner is irrelevant?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would argue that you could make a -- you could make a claim that none of that donning and doffing ought to be compensable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: But you're saying -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chamber of Commerce",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "as the Chamber of Commerce brief says, that is precisely what we're talking about here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0001-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are collateral consequences to deciding what the Federal law issue is in this particular context."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it so that collective bargaining could not trade off the compensation for the walking and the donning and doffing for some other benefit that the employees might prefer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: So, you say it's an open question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. GOLDSTEIN",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0002-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court denied certiorari on that question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. GOLDSTEIN",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "case that's confronted this, which is the Metzler case, 127 F.3d 959."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. GOLDSTEIN",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Walking and waiting time has been held compensable since at least 1961. The Mitchell case, 286 F.2d 721, the Barrentine case, 750 F.2d 47."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Portal Act excludes walking time from compensation only when it occurs outside the workday, before an employee commences, or after he ceases, his principal activities. And Steiner held that the term \"principal activities\" includes activities that are an integral and indispensable part of the principal activities. It follows that when donning and doffing are integral and indispensable parts of the principal activities of the employees, then walking that occurs after donning, and before doffing, occurs within the workday, and it is not excluded from compensation by the Portal Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Employers",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, the employers in these cases have argued that the term \"principal activities\" does not encompass activities that are integral and indispensable parts thereof, and that Steiner did not so hold."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gornstein",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORNSTEIN: -- certiorari as an issue that can be, and should be, resolved, in our view. But if the Court doesn't want to resolve that issue, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: -- why, in all these years, hasn't the Department of Labor gotten rid of it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Carter G. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Their position -\u00ad Justice Ginsburg -- or, no Justice O'Connor specifically asked that question, \"You're not saying that waiting time prior to engaging in a primary activity, in fact, starts the workday.\" And the answer is, absolutely, it does, because"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gornstein",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORNSTEIN: It should have. Because even at the time it was written, that reservation was in tension or not in conflict with the plain language of the regulations. And certainly by the time of Steiner, it was clear that this kind of time was compensable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: Was the predonning waiting issue decided below?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Well, it seems the court below said waiting time isn't covered, so we're not going to engage in any debate about what -- if waiting time is \u00ad - were covered, which waiting time?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0003-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "With respect to the holding of Steiner -- I mean, it's important to put in mind, Steiner -- one of the things -- two things that Steiner focused on -- it focused on section 3.0, and it recognized that there are going to be situations where you're going to be able to bargain away clothes changing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0003-0007",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "compensable. That's an absurd outcome in a situation where Congress clearly had one thing in mind that it absolutely wanted to accomplish, and that was to ensure that walking, riding, traveling to the place where you actually perform the services for which you've been hired, has been -- has -- is excluded from being mandatorily compensated -- Steiner doesn't deal with 4(a)(1); the language is as plain as it can be -- are not -- you know, unless specifically excluded by section 4(a)(1)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-03-1238",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1cba6ea47e4170013b22779fcddb371e961acbb9cf35b842fd3d5d7be53b45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1cba6ea47e-0003-0008",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
